  "transcript": {
    "answer": "Because of fetch's timeout on response headers. The code comment in lore-api-backfill.ts says fetch gives up on a response whose headers take more than five minutes. lore-api only answers a big repo's backfill once every document is in, so the response can take longer than that. The spec (FR7.9) has each call wait up to 30 minutes for the answer, which fetch can't do. node:http (or node:https) lets the sweep wait that long.",
